<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>How</title>
</head>
<body><font><span>Depending on the institution where you study, you can often gain experience with transdisciplinary education as a student. Various universities and colleges offer transdisciplinary courses, modules, minors, or honors programs. These programs focus on working on a complex societal issue—students work together with parties outside education on a question. Examples (from the Netherlands) include the </span> <a href="https://www.valuecreators-whc.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Value Creators program</span></a> <span> at Windesheim, De Tussenruimte at Avans, and the </span> <a href="https://www.utwente.nl/en/education/master/programmes/transdisciplinary-master-insert/" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><span>Shaping Responsible Futures</span></a>&nbsp;<span>master at the University of Twente.</span></font></body>
</html>